/-!
# The free rigid monoidal category on a duality signature

A *duality signature* (`TauCeti.DualitySignature`) consists of a type of generating objects and a
type of generating morphisms (*coupons*), each coupon having a source and a target which are formal
rigid object expressions (`TauCeti.RigidObject`) built from the generating objects using the unit,
tensor product, right dual and left dual. Thus coupon boundaries may involve iterated right and left
duals as well as empty or multi-port tensor words, while `TensorSignature.toDualitySignature`
embeds ordinary dual-free tensor signatures.

The free rigid (autonomous) monoidal category `DualitySignature.FreeRigid S` on a duality signature
`S` has `RigidObject S.Obj` as objects. Its morphisms are formal composites, tensor products and
whiskerings of identities, associators, unitors, right and left coevaluations and evaluations, and
coupons, quotiented by the congruence `FreeRigid.HomEquiv` generated by the monoidal-category axioms
together with the four zigzag (snake) equations of `CategoryTheory.ExactPairing`. No pivotal
identification `X ≅ Xᘁᘁ` and no equation between coupons is imposed.

## Main definitions and results

* `TauCeti.RigidObject.projectObj`: interpret formal rigid object expressions in an arbitrary
  rigid monoidal category, compatibly with `FreeMonoidalCategory.projectObj` via
  `RigidObject.projectObj_toRigidObject`.
* `TauCeti.DualitySignature` and `TauCeti.TensorSignature.toDualitySignature`: duality signatures
  with `RigidObject` boundaries and the inclusion of dual-free tensor signatures.
* `TauCeti.DualitySignature.FreeRigid S`: the free rigid monoidal category on `S`, equipped with
  `Category`, `MonoidalCategory`, `RightRigidCategory`, `LeftRigidCategory` and `RigidCategory`
  instances, generators `FreeRigid.of` and `FreeRigid.coupon`, morphism induction
  `FreeRigid.Hom.inductionOn`, and strong monoidal inclusion
  `TensorSignature.FreeMonoidal.toFreeRigid`.
* `FreeRigid.lift fo fc`: the universal strong monoidal functor into an arbitrary (not necessarily
  strict) rigid monoidal category `D`, with identity unit and tensor comparisons and identity dual
  comparisons `FreeRigid.lift_mapRightDualIso` and `FreeRigid.lift_mapLeftDualIso`.
* `FreeRigid.natTrans_ext` and `FreeRigid.monoidalNatIso`: monoidal natural transformations from a
  strong monoidal functor to a lax monoidal functor out of `S.FreeRigid` are determined by the
  generating objects, and two strong monoidal functors into a rigid category that agree up to
  isomorphism on generating objects compatibly with coupons are uniquely monoidally naturally
  isomorphic.
* `FreeRigid.isEmpty_hom_of_doubleRightDual`, `FreeRigid.isEmpty_hom_doubleRightDual_of`,
  `FreeRigid.isEmpty_iso_of_doubleRightDual` (and their left-dual counterparts): in the free rigid
  category on a coupon-free signature, there is no morphism in either direction between a generating
  object `of a` and its double right dual `((of a)ᘁ)ᘁ` or double left dual `ᘁ(ᘁ(of a))`, witnessing
  that autonomous coherence does not collapse double duals without a pivotal structure.

## Design notes and attribution

The quotient construction of `FreeRigid`, its universal lift and its monoidal natural isomorphism
parallel `TauCeti.TensorSignature.FreeMonoidal` (modeled on Markus Himmel's
`Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Free/Basic.lean`), extended by right and left (co)evaluation
constructors and the zigzag axioms of Jakob von Raumer's `CategoryTheory.ExactPairing`
(`Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Rigid/Basic.lean`). The non-pivotal separation model adapts
Joachim Lambek's pregroup of periodic monotone integer maps under Galois adjunction.

## References

* A. Joyal and R. Street, *The geometry of tensor calculus I*, Adv. Math. 88 (1991).
* A. Joyal and R. Street, *Planar diagrams and tensor algebra*, unpublished manuscript (1988).
* P. Selinger, *A survey of graphical languages for monoidal categories*, New Structures for
  Physics, Lecture Notes in Phys. 813 (2011), §4.
* J. Lambek, *Type grammar revisited*, Logical Aspects of Computational Linguistics (LACL 1997),
  Lecture Notes in Comput. Sci. 1582 (1999), 1–27.
-/

public section

universe u v u' v'

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory ExactPairing

namespace TauCeti

namespace RigidObject

section ProjectObj

variable {α : Type u} {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [MonoidalCategory D] [RigidCategory D]

/-- Interpret a formal rigid object expression in a rigid monoidal category `D`, sending `.of a` to
`f a`, `.unit` to `𝟙_ D`, `.tensor` to tensor product, `.rightDual` to the chosen right dual, and
`.leftDual` to the chosen left dual. Exposed so dependent morphism types over interpreted boundaries
reduce on constructors, matching `FreeMonoidalCategory.projectObj`. -/
@[expose] noncomputable def projectObj (f : α → D) : RigidObject α → D
  | .of a => f a
  | .unit => 𝟙_ D
  | .tensor X Y => projectObj f X ⊗ projectObj f Y
  | .rightDual X => (projectObj f X)ᘁ
  | .leftDual X => ᘁ(projectObj f X)

@[simp]
theorem projectObj_of (f : α → D) (a : α) : projectObj f (.of a) = f a := rfl

@[simp]
theorem projectObj_unit (f : α → D) : projectObj f .unit = 𝟙_ D := rfl

@[simp]
theorem projectObj_tensor (f : α → D) (X Y : RigidObject α) :
    projectObj f (X.tensor Y) = projectObj f X ⊗ projectObj f Y := rfl

@[simp]
theorem projectObj_rightDual (f : α → D) (X : RigidObject α) :
    projectObj f X.rightDual = (projectObj f X)ᘁ := rfl

@[simp]
theorem projectObj_leftDual (f : α → D) (X : RigidObject α) :
    projectObj f X.leftDual = ᘁ(projectObj f X) := rfl

/-- Interpreting a dual-free monoidal word after embedding into `RigidObject` agrees with Mathlib's
`FreeMonoidalCategory.projectObj`. -/
@[simp]
theorem projectObj_toRigidObject (f : α → D) (W : FreeMonoidalCategory α) :
    projectObj f W.toRigidObject = FreeMonoidalCategory.projectObj f W := by
  induction W <;> simp_all [FreeMonoidalCategory.projectObj]

end ProjectObj

end RigidObject

/-- A duality signature: a type `Obj` of generating objects and a type `Coupon` of generating
morphisms, each coupon having a source and a target formal rigid object expression in `Obj`. -/
structure DualitySignature where
  /-- The generating objects. -/
  Obj : Type u
  /-- The generating morphisms (coupons). -/
  Coupon : Type v
  /-- The source rigid object expression of a coupon. -/
  src : Coupon → RigidObject Obj
  /-- The target rigid object expression of a coupon. -/
  tgt : Coupon → RigidObject Obj

/-- View an ordinary dual-free tensor signature as a duality signature by embedding its formal
tensor-word boundaries into `RigidObject`. -/
@[expose] def TensorSignature.toDualitySignature (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) :
    DualitySignature.{u, v} where
  Obj := S.Obj
  Coupon := S.Coupon
  src g := (S.src g).toRigidObject
  tgt g := (S.tgt g).toRigidObject

@[simp]
theorem TensorSignature.toDualitySignature_obj (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) :
    S.toDualitySignature.Obj = S.Obj := rfl

@[simp]
theorem TensorSignature.toDualitySignature_coupon (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) :
    S.toDualitySignature.Coupon = S.Coupon := rfl

@[simp]
theorem TensorSignature.toDualitySignature_src (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) (g : S.Coupon) :
    S.toDualitySignature.src g = (S.src g).toRigidObject := rfl

@[simp]
theorem TensorSignature.toDualitySignature_tgt (S : TensorSignature.{u, v}) (g : S.Coupon) :
    S.toDualitySignature.tgt g = (S.tgt g).toRigidObject := rfl

namespace DualitySignature

variable (S : DualitySignature.{u, v})

/-- The free rigid monoidal category on a duality signature `S`. Its objects are the formal rigid
object expressions `RigidObject S.Obj`. -/
@[ext]
structure FreeRigid where
  /-- The formal rigid object expression underlying an object of `S.FreeRigid`. -/
  as : RigidObject S.Obj

namespace FreeRigid

variable {S}

/-- The object of `S.FreeRigid` given by a single generating object. -/
@[expose] def of (a : S.Obj) : S.FreeRigid := ⟨.of a⟩

/-- Formal morphism expressions of the free rigid category on `S`: identities, associators, unitors,
right and left coevaluations and evaluations, and coupons, closed under composition, whiskering and
tensor product. -/
inductive Hom : RigidObject S.Obj → RigidObject S.Obj → Type (max u v)
  | id (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom X X
  | α_hom (X Y Z : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom ((X.tensor Y).tensor Z) (X.tensor (Y.tensor Z))
  | α_inv (X Y Z : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom (X.tensor (Y.tensor Z)) ((X.tensor Y).tensor Z)
  | l_hom (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom (RigidObject.unit.tensor X) X
  | l_inv (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom X (RigidObject.unit.tensor X)
  | ρ_hom (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom (X.tensor RigidObject.unit) X
  | ρ_inv (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom X (X.tensor RigidObject.unit)
  | rightCoevaluation (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom RigidObject.unit (X.tensor X.rightDual)
  | rightEvaluation (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom (X.rightDual.tensor X) RigidObject.unit
  | leftCoevaluation (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom RigidObject.unit (X.leftDual.tensor X)
  | leftEvaluation (X : RigidObject S.Obj) : Hom (X.tensor X.leftDual) RigidObject.unit
  | coupon (g : S.Coupon) : Hom (S.src g) (S.tgt g)
  | comp {X Y Z} (f : Hom X Y) (g : Hom Y Z) : Hom X Z
  | whiskerLeft (X : RigidObject S.Obj) {Y₁ Y₂} (f : Hom Y₁ Y₂) :
      Hom (X.tensor Y₁) (X.tensor Y₂)
  | whiskerRight {X₁ X₂} (f : Hom X₁ X₂) (Y : RigidObject S.Obj) :
      Hom (X₁.tensor Y) (X₂.tensor Y)
  | tensor {W X Y Z} (f : Hom W Y) (g : Hom X Z) : Hom (W.tensor X) (Y.tensor Z)

/-- The congruence on formal morphism expressions generated by the axioms of a monoidal category and
the four zigzag equations of right and left duality. No pivotal relation or coupon equation is
imposed. -/
inductive HomEquiv : ∀ {X Y : RigidObject S.Obj}, Hom X Y → Hom X Y → Prop
  | refl {X Y} (f : Hom X Y) : HomEquiv f f
  | symm {X Y} (f g : Hom X Y) : HomEquiv f g → HomEquiv g f
  | trans {X Y} {f g h : Hom X Y} : HomEquiv f g → HomEquiv g h → HomEquiv f h
  | comp {X Y Z} {f f' : Hom X Y} {g g' : Hom Y Z} :
      HomEquiv f f' → HomEquiv g g' → HomEquiv (f.comp g) (f'.comp g')
  | whiskerLeft (X) {Y Z} (f f' : Hom Y Z) :
      HomEquiv f f' → HomEquiv (f.whiskerLeft X) (f'.whiskerLeft X)
  | whiskerRight {Y Z} (f f' : Hom Y Z) (X) :
      HomEquiv f f' → HomEquiv (f.whiskerRight X) (f'.whiskerRight X)
  | tensor {W X Y Z} {f f' : Hom W X} {g g' : Hom Y Z} :
      HomEquiv f f' → HomEquiv g g' → HomEquiv (f.tensor g) (f'.tensor g')
  | tensorHom_def {X₁ Y₁ X₂ Y₂} (f : Hom X₁ Y₁) (g : Hom X₂ Y₂) :
      HomEquiv (f.tensor g) ((f.whiskerRight X₂).comp (g.whiskerLeft Y₁))
  | comp_id {X Y} (f : Hom X Y) : HomEquiv (f.comp (Hom.id _)) f
  | id_comp {X Y} (f : Hom X Y) : HomEquiv ((Hom.id _).comp f) f
  | assoc {X Y U V} (f : Hom X U) (g : Hom U V) (h : Hom V Y) :
      HomEquiv ((f.comp g).comp h) (f.comp (g.comp h))
  | id_tensorHom_id {X Y} : HomEquiv ((Hom.id X).tensor (Hom.id Y)) (Hom.id _)
  | tensorHom_comp_tensorHom {X₁ Y₁ Z₁ X₂ Y₂ Z₂} (f₁ : Hom X₁ Y₁) (f₂ : Hom X₂ Y₂)
      (g₁ : Hom Y₁ Z₁) (g₂ : Hom Y₂ Z₂) :
      HomEquiv ((f₁.tensor f₂).comp (g₁.tensor g₂)) ((f₁.comp g₁).tensor (f₂.comp g₂))
  | whiskerLeft_id (X Y) : HomEquiv ((Hom.id Y).whiskerLeft X) (Hom.id (X.tensor Y))
  | id_whiskerRight (X Y) : HomEquiv ((Hom.id X).whiskerRight Y) (Hom.id (X.tensor Y))
  | α_hom_inv {X Y Z} : HomEquiv ((Hom.α_hom X Y Z).comp (Hom.α_inv X Y Z)) (Hom.id _)
  | α_inv_hom {X Y Z} : HomEquiv ((Hom.α_inv X Y Z).comp (Hom.α_hom X Y Z)) (Hom.id _)
  | associator_naturality {X₁ X₂ X₃ Y₁ Y₂ Y₃} (f₁ : Hom X₁ Y₁) (f₂ : Hom X₂ Y₂)
      (f₃ : Hom X₃ Y₃) :
      HomEquiv (((f₁.tensor f₂).tensor f₃).comp (Hom.α_hom Y₁ Y₂ Y₃))
        ((Hom.α_hom X₁ X₂ X₃).comp (f₁.tensor (f₂.tensor f₃)))
  | ρ_hom_inv {X} : HomEquiv ((Hom.ρ_hom X).comp (Hom.ρ_inv X)) (Hom.id _)
  | ρ_inv_hom {X} : HomEquiv ((Hom.ρ_inv X).comp (Hom.ρ_hom X)) (Hom.id _)
  | ρ_naturality {X Y} (f : Hom X Y) :
      HomEquiv ((f.whiskerRight .unit).comp (Hom.ρ_hom Y)) ((Hom.ρ_hom X).comp f)
  | l_hom_inv {X} : HomEquiv ((Hom.l_hom X).comp (Hom.l_inv X)) (Hom.id _)
  | l_inv_hom {X} : HomEquiv ((Hom.l_inv X).comp (Hom.l_hom X)) (Hom.id _)
  | l_naturality {X Y} (f : Hom X Y) :
      HomEquiv ((f.whiskerLeft .unit).comp (Hom.l_hom Y)) ((Hom.l_hom X).comp f)
  | pentagon {W X Y Z} :
      HomEquiv
        (((Hom.α_hom W X Y).whiskerRight Z).comp
          ((Hom.α_hom W (X.tensor Y) Z).comp ((Hom.α_hom X Y Z).whiskerLeft W)))
        ((Hom.α_hom (W.tensor X) Y Z).comp (Hom.α_hom W X (Y.tensor Z)))
  | triangle {X Y} :
      HomEquiv ((Hom.α_hom X .unit Y).comp ((Hom.l_hom Y).whiskerLeft X))
        ((Hom.ρ_hom X).whiskerRight Y)
  | right_coevaluation_evaluation (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
      HomEquiv
        (((Hom.rightCoevaluation X).whiskerLeft X.rightDual).comp
          ((Hom.α_inv X.rightDual X X.rightDual).comp
            ((Hom.rightEvaluation X).whiskerRight X.rightDual)))
        ((Hom.ρ_hom X.rightDual).comp (Hom.l_inv X.rightDual))
  | right_evaluation_coevaluation (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
      HomEquiv
        (((Hom.rightCoevaluation X).whiskerRight X).comp
          ((Hom.α_hom X X.rightDual X).comp ((Hom.rightEvaluation X).whiskerLeft X)))
        ((Hom.l_hom X).comp (Hom.ρ_inv X))
  | left_coevaluation_evaluation (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
      HomEquiv
        (((Hom.leftCoevaluation X).whiskerLeft X).comp
          ((Hom.α_inv X X.leftDual X).comp ((Hom.leftEvaluation X).whiskerRight X)))
        ((Hom.ρ_hom X).comp (Hom.l_inv X))
  | left_evaluation_coevaluation (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
      HomEquiv
        (((Hom.leftCoevaluation X).whiskerRight X.leftDual).comp
          ((Hom.α_hom X.leftDual X X.leftDual).comp
            ((Hom.leftEvaluation X).whiskerLeft X.leftDual)))
        ((Hom.l_hom X.leftDual).comp (Hom.ρ_inv X.leftDual))

/-- Formal morphism expressions are identified when the monoidal and zigzag axioms equate them. -/
instance setoidHom (X Y : RigidObject S.Obj) : Setoid (Hom X Y) :=
  ⟨HomEquiv, ⟨HomEquiv.refl, HomEquiv.symm _ _, HomEquiv.trans⟩⟩

section Instances

open HomEquiv

instance : Category.{max u v} S.FreeRigid where
  Hom X Y := Quotient (setoidHom X.as Y.as)
  id X := ⟦Hom.id X.as⟧
  comp := Quotient.map₂ Hom.comp (fun _ _ hf _ _ hg ↦ HomEquiv.comp hf hg)
  id_comp := by
    rintro X Y ⟨f⟩
    exact Quotient.sound (id_comp f)
  comp_id := by
    rintro X Y ⟨f⟩
    exact Quotient.sound (comp_id f)
  assoc := by
    rintro W X Y Z ⟨f⟩ ⟨g⟩ ⟨h⟩
    exact Quotient.sound (assoc f g h)

instance : MonoidalCategory S.FreeRigid where
  tensorObj X Y := ⟨X.as.tensor Y.as⟩
  tensorHom := Quotient.map₂ Hom.tensor (fun _ _ hf _ _ hg ↦ HomEquiv.tensor hf hg)
  whiskerLeft X _ _ f :=
    Quot.map (fun f ↦ Hom.whiskerLeft X.as f) (fun f f' ↦ .whiskerLeft _ f f') f
  whiskerRight f Y :=
    Quot.map (fun f ↦ Hom.whiskerRight f Y.as) (fun f f' ↦ .whiskerRight f f' _) f
  tensorHom_def := by
    rintro _ _ _ _ ⟨f⟩ ⟨g⟩
    exact Quotient.sound (tensorHom_def _ _)
  id_tensorHom_id _ _ := Quot.sound id_tensorHom_id
  tensorHom_comp_tensorHom := by
    rintro _ _ _ _ _ _ ⟨f₁⟩ ⟨f₂⟩ ⟨g₁⟩ ⟨g₂⟩
    exact Quotient.sound (tensorHom_comp_tensorHom _ _ _ _)
  whiskerLeft_id X Y := Quot.sound (HomEquiv.whiskerLeft_id X.as Y.as)
  id_whiskerRight X Y := Quot.sound (HomEquiv.id_whiskerRight X.as Y.as)
  tensorUnit := ⟨.unit⟩
  associator X Y Z :=
    ⟨⟦Hom.α_hom X.as Y.as Z.as⟧, ⟦Hom.α_inv X.as Y.as Z.as⟧, Quotient.sound α_hom_inv,
      Quotient.sound α_inv_hom⟩
  associator_naturality := by
    rintro _ _ _ _ _ _ ⟨f₁⟩ ⟨f₂⟩ ⟨f₃⟩
    exact Quotient.sound (associator_naturality _ _ _)
  leftUnitor X :=
    ⟨⟦Hom.l_hom X.as⟧, ⟦Hom.l_inv X.as⟧, Quotient.sound l_hom_inv, Quotient.sound l_inv_hom⟩
  leftUnitor_naturality := by
    rintro _ _ ⟨f⟩
    exact Quotient.sound (l_naturality _)
  rightUnitor X :=
    ⟨⟦Hom.ρ_hom X.as⟧, ⟦Hom.ρ_inv X.as⟧, Quotient.sound ρ_hom_inv, Quotient.sound ρ_inv_hom⟩
  rightUnitor_naturality := by
    rintro _ _ ⟨f⟩
    exact Quotient.sound (ρ_naturality _)
  pentagon _ _ _ _ := Quotient.sound pentagon
  triangle _ _ := Quotient.sound triangle

instance : RightRigidCategory S.FreeRigid where
  rightDual X :=
    { rightDual := ⟨X.as.rightDual⟩
      exact :=
        { coevaluation' := ⟦Hom.rightCoevaluation X.as⟧
          evaluation' := ⟦Hom.rightEvaluation X.as⟧
          coevaluation_evaluation' := Quotient.sound (right_coevaluation_evaluation X.as)
          evaluation_coevaluation' := Quotient.sound (right_evaluation_coevaluation X.as) } }

instance : LeftRigidCategory S.FreeRigid where
  leftDual X :=
    { leftDual := ⟨X.as.leftDual⟩
      exact :=
        { coevaluation' := ⟦Hom.leftCoevaluation X.as⟧
          evaluation' := ⟦Hom.leftEvaluation X.as⟧
          coevaluation_evaluation' := Quotient.sound (left_coevaluation_evaluation X.as)
          evaluation_coevaluation' := Quotient.sound (left_evaluation_coevaluation X.as) } }

instance : RigidCategory S.FreeRigid where

end Instances

theorem as_of (a : S.Obj) : (of a).as = .of a := rfl

theorem as_tensorUnit : (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as = .unit := rfl

theorem as_tensor (X Y : S.FreeRigid) : (X ⊗ Y).as = X.as.tensor Y.as := rfl

theorem as_rightDual (X : S.FreeRigid) : (Xᘁ).as = X.as.rightDual := rfl

theorem as_leftDual (X : S.FreeRigid) : (ᘁX).as = X.as.leftDual := rfl

/-- Interpreting a formal rigid object expression via the generating objects of `S.FreeRigid`
recovers the object wrapping that expression. -/
@[simp]
theorem projectObj_of_eq (X : RigidObject S.Obj) :
    RigidObject.projectObj (of (S := S)) X = ⟨X⟩ := by
  induction X with
  | of _ => rfl
  | unit => rfl
  | tensor _ _ ihX ihY =>
    dsimp only [RigidObject.projectObj]
    rw [ihX, ihY]
    rfl
  | rightDual _ ihX =>
    dsimp only [RigidObject.projectObj]
    rw [ihX]
    rfl
  | leftDual _ ihX =>
    dsimp only [RigidObject.projectObj]
    rw [ihX]
    rfl

/-- The morphism of `S.FreeRigid` represented by a formal morphism expression. -/
abbrev homMk {X Y : S.FreeRigid} (f : Hom X.as Y.as) : X ⟶ Y := ⟦f⟧

/-- The generating morphism given by a coupon, from its source rigid expression to its target rigid
expression. -/
@[expose] def coupon (g : S.Coupon) : (⟨S.src g⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ⟶ ⟨S.tgt g⟩ :=
  homMk (Hom.coupon g)

@[simp]
theorem homMk_id (X : S.FreeRigid) : homMk (Hom.id X.as) = 𝟙 X := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_comp {X Y Z : S.FreeRigid} (f : Hom X.as Y.as) (g : Hom Y.as Z.as) :
    homMk (Y := Z) (f.comp g) = homMk f ≫ homMk g := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_tensor {X₁ Y₁ X₂ Y₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : Hom X₁.as Y₁.as) (g : Hom X₂.as Y₂.as) :
    homMk (X := X₁ ⊗ X₂) (Y := Y₁ ⊗ Y₂) (f.tensor g) = homMk f ⊗ₘ homMk g := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_whiskerLeft (X : S.FreeRigid) {Y₁ Y₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : Hom Y₁.as Y₂.as) :
    homMk (X := X ⊗ Y₁) (Y := X ⊗ Y₂) (f.whiskerLeft X.as) = X ◁ homMk f := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_whiskerRight {X₁ X₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : Hom X₁.as X₂.as) (Y : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := X₁ ⊗ Y) (Y := X₂ ⊗ Y) (f.whiskerRight Y.as) = homMk f ▷ Y := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_α_hom (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := (X ⊗ Y) ⊗ Z) (Y := X ⊗ (Y ⊗ Z)) (Hom.α_hom X.as Y.as Z.as) = (α_ X Y Z).hom :=
  rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_α_inv (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := X ⊗ (Y ⊗ Z)) (Y := (X ⊗ Y) ⊗ Z) (Hom.α_inv X.as Y.as Z.as) = (α_ X Y Z).inv :=
  rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_l_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := 𝟙_ _ ⊗ X) (Hom.l_hom X.as) = (λ_ X).hom := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_l_inv (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (Y := 𝟙_ _ ⊗ X) (Hom.l_inv X.as) = (λ_ X).inv := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_ρ_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := X ⊗ 𝟙_ _) (Hom.ρ_hom X.as) = (ρ_ X).hom := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_ρ_inv (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (Y := X ⊗ 𝟙_ _) (Hom.ρ_inv X.as) = (ρ_ X).inv := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_rightCoevaluation (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := 𝟙_ _) (Y := X ⊗ Xᘁ) (Hom.rightCoevaluation X.as) = η_ X (Xᘁ) := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_rightEvaluation (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := Xᘁ ⊗ X) (Y := 𝟙_ _) (Hom.rightEvaluation X.as) = ε_ X (Xᘁ) := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_leftCoevaluation (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := 𝟙_ _) (Y := (ᘁX) ⊗ X) (Hom.leftCoevaluation X.as) = η_ (ᘁX) X := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_leftEvaluation (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    homMk (X := X ⊗ (ᘁX)) (Y := 𝟙_ _) (Hom.leftEvaluation X.as) = ε_ (ᘁX) X := rfl

@[simp]
theorem homMk_coupon (g : S.Coupon) :
    homMk (X := ⟨S.src g⟩) (Y := ⟨S.tgt g⟩) (Hom.coupon g) = coupon g := rfl

/-- Induction principle for morphisms of the free rigid category: a property of morphisms holding
for identities, associators, unitors, right and left coevaluations and evaluations, and coupons,
and stable under composition and whiskering on either side, holds for every morphism. -/
theorem Hom.inductionOn {motive : {X Y : S.FreeRigid} → (X ⟶ Y) → Prop} {X Y : S.FreeRigid}
    (t : X ⟶ Y)
    (id : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (𝟙 X))
    (α_hom : (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) → motive (α_ X Y Z).hom)
    (α_inv : (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) → motive (α_ X Y Z).inv)
    (l_hom : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (λ_ X).hom)
    (l_inv : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (λ_ X).inv)
    (ρ_hom : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (ρ_ X).hom)
    (ρ_inv : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (ρ_ X).inv)
    (rightCoevaluation : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (η_ X (Xᘁ)))
    (rightEvaluation : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (ε_ X (Xᘁ)))
    (leftCoevaluation : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (η_ (ᘁX) X))
    (leftEvaluation : (X : S.FreeRigid) → motive (ε_ (ᘁX) X))
    (coupon : (g : S.Coupon) → motive (FreeRigid.coupon g))
    (comp : {X Y Z : S.FreeRigid} → (f : X ⟶ Y) → (g : Y ⟶ Z) → motive f → motive g →
      motive (f ≫ g))
    (whiskerLeft : (X : S.FreeRigid) → {Y Z : S.FreeRigid} → (f : Y ⟶ Z) → motive f →
      motive (X ◁ f))
    (whiskerRight : {X Y : S.FreeRigid} → (f : X ⟶ Y) → (Z : S.FreeRigid) → motive f →
      motive (f ▷ Z)) :
    motive t := by
  suffices H : ∀ {X Y : RigidObject S.Obj} (f : Hom X Y),
      motive (homMk (X := ⟨X⟩) (Y := ⟨Y⟩) f) by
    induction t using Quotient.inductionOn with | _ f
    exact H f
  intro X Y f
  induction f with
  | id X => exact id ⟨X⟩
  | α_hom X Y Z => exact α_hom ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩ ⟨Z⟩
  | α_inv X Y Z => exact α_inv ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩ ⟨Z⟩
  | l_hom X => exact l_hom ⟨X⟩
  | l_inv X => exact l_inv ⟨X⟩
  | ρ_hom X => exact ρ_hom ⟨X⟩
  | ρ_inv X => exact ρ_inv ⟨X⟩
  | rightCoevaluation X => exact rightCoevaluation ⟨X⟩
  | rightEvaluation X => exact rightEvaluation ⟨X⟩
  | leftCoevaluation X => exact leftCoevaluation ⟨X⟩
  | leftEvaluation X => exact leftEvaluation ⟨X⟩
  | coupon g => exact coupon g
  | comp f g hf hg => exact comp _ _ hf hg
  | whiskerLeft X f hf => exact whiskerLeft ⟨X⟩ _ hf
  | whiskerRight f X hf => exact whiskerRight _ ⟨X⟩ hf
  | @tensor W X Y Z f g hf hg =>
    have h : (homMk (f.tensor g) : (⟨W.tensor X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ⟶ ⟨Y.tensor Z⟩) =
        homMk (X := ⟨W⟩) (Y := ⟨Y⟩) f ▷ (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ≫
          (⟨Y⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ◁ homMk (X := ⟨X⟩) (Y := ⟨Z⟩) g :=
      Quotient.sound (HomEquiv.tensorHom_def f g)
    rw [h]
    exact comp _ _ (whiskerRight _ _ hf) (whiskerLeft _ _ hg)

section Lift

variable {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [MonoidalCategory D] [RigidCategory D] (fo : S.Obj → D)
  (fc : ∀ g : S.Coupon, RigidObject.projectObj fo (S.src g) ⟶ RigidObject.projectObj fo (S.tgt g))

/-- Interpret a formal morphism expression in `D`, given interpretations `fo` of generating objects
and `fc` of coupons. Auxiliary definition for `FreeRigid.liftMap`. -/
private noncomputable def liftMapAux :
    ∀ {X Y : RigidObject S.Obj}, Hom X Y →
      (RigidObject.projectObj fo X ⟶ RigidObject.projectObj fo Y)
  | _, _, Hom.id _ => 𝟙 _
  | _, _, Hom.α_hom _ _ _ => (α_ _ _ _).hom
  | _, _, Hom.α_inv _ _ _ => (α_ _ _ _).inv
  | _, _, Hom.l_hom _ => (λ_ _).hom
  | _, _, Hom.l_inv _ => (λ_ _).inv
  | _, _, Hom.ρ_hom _ => (ρ_ _).hom
  | _, _, Hom.ρ_inv _ => (ρ_ _).inv
  | _, _, Hom.rightCoevaluation X =>
    η_ (RigidObject.projectObj fo X) ((RigidObject.projectObj fo X)ᘁ)
  | _, _, Hom.rightEvaluation X =>
    ε_ (RigidObject.projectObj fo X) ((RigidObject.projectObj fo X)ᘁ)
  | _, _, Hom.leftCoevaluation X =>
    η_ (ᘁ(RigidObject.projectObj fo X)) (RigidObject.projectObj fo X)
  | _, _, Hom.leftEvaluation X =>
    ε_ (ᘁ(RigidObject.projectObj fo X)) (RigidObject.projectObj fo X)
  | _, _, Hom.coupon g => fc g
  | _, _, Hom.comp f g => liftMapAux f ≫ liftMapAux g
  | _, _, Hom.whiskerLeft X p => RigidObject.projectObj fo X ◁ liftMapAux p
  | _, _, Hom.whiskerRight p X => liftMapAux p ▷ RigidObject.projectObj fo X
  | _, _, Hom.tensor f g => liftMapAux f ⊗ₘ liftMapAux g

/-- The interpretation of formal morphism expressions respects the monoidal and zigzag axioms. -/
private theorem liftMapAux_sound {X Y : RigidObject S.Obj} {f g : Hom X Y} (h : HomEquiv f g) :
    liftMapAux fo fc f = liftMapAux fo fc g := by
  induction h with
  | refl => rfl
  | symm _ _ _ hfg => exact hfg.symm
  | trans _ _ hfg hgh => exact hfg.trans hgh
  | comp _ _ hf hg => simp only [liftMapAux, hf, hg]
  | whiskerLeft _ _ _ _ hf => dsimp only [liftMapAux]; rw [hf]
  | whiskerRight _ _ _ _ hf => dsimp only [liftMapAux]; rw [hf]
  | tensor _ _ hf hg => dsimp only [liftMapAux]; rw [hf, hg]
  | tensorHom_def => exact MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def _ _
  | comp_id => exact Category.comp_id _
  | id_comp => exact Category.id_comp _
  | assoc => exact Category.assoc _ _ _
  | id_tensorHom_id => exact MonoidalCategory.id_tensorHom_id _ _
  | tensorHom_comp_tensorHom => exact MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_comp_tensorHom _ _ _ _
  | whiskerLeft_id => exact MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_id _ _
  | id_whiskerRight => exact MonoidalCategory.id_whiskerRight _ _
  | α_hom_inv => exact Iso.hom_inv_id _
  | α_inv_hom => exact Iso.inv_hom_id _
  | associator_naturality => exact MonoidalCategory.associator_naturality _ _ _
  | ρ_hom_inv => exact Iso.hom_inv_id _
  | ρ_inv_hom => exact Iso.inv_hom_id _
  | ρ_naturality => exact MonoidalCategory.rightUnitor_naturality _
  | l_hom_inv => exact Iso.hom_inv_id _
  | l_inv_hom => exact Iso.inv_hom_id _
  | l_naturality => exact MonoidalCategory.leftUnitor_naturality _
  | pentagon => exact MonoidalCategory.pentagon _ _ _ _
  | triangle => exact MonoidalCategory.triangle _ _
  | right_coevaluation_evaluation X =>
    exact ExactPairing.coevaluation_evaluation
      (RigidObject.projectObj fo X) ((RigidObject.projectObj fo X)ᘁ)
  | right_evaluation_coevaluation X =>
    exact ExactPairing.evaluation_coevaluation
      (RigidObject.projectObj fo X) ((RigidObject.projectObj fo X)ᘁ)
  | left_coevaluation_evaluation X =>
    exact ExactPairing.coevaluation_evaluation
      (ᘁ(RigidObject.projectObj fo X)) (RigidObject.projectObj fo X)
  | left_evaluation_coevaluation X =>
    exact ExactPairing.evaluation_coevaluation
      (ᘁ(RigidObject.projectObj fo X)) (RigidObject.projectObj fo X)

/-- The interpretation of morphisms of `S.FreeRigid`, given the images `fo` of generating objects
and `fc` of coupons. This is the morphism map of `FreeRigid.lift`; compute it via the `lift_map_*`
lemmas. -/
noncomputable def liftMap {X Y : S.FreeRigid} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    RigidObject.projectObj fo X.as ⟶ RigidObject.projectObj fo Y.as :=
  Quotient.lift (liftMapAux fo fc) (fun _ _ h ↦ liftMapAux_sound fo fc h) f

theorem liftMap_id (X : S.FreeRigid) : liftMap fo fc (𝟙 X) = 𝟙 _ := by rfl

theorem liftMap_comp {X Y Z : S.FreeRigid} (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Y ⟶ Z) :
    liftMap fo fc (f ≫ g) = liftMap fo fc f ≫ liftMap fo fc g := by
  induction f using Quotient.inductionOn
  induction g using Quotient.inductionOn
  rfl

/-- The universal strong monoidal functor out of `S.FreeRigid` into an arbitrary rigid monoidal
category `D`, determined by the images `fo` of generating objects and `fc` of coupons. Its unit,
tensor and dual comparison isomorphisms are all identities. -/
@[expose] noncomputable def lift : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D where
  obj X := RigidObject.projectObj fo X.as
  map := liftMap fo fc
  map_id := liftMap_id fo fc
  map_comp := liftMap_comp fo fc

@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_of (a : S.Obj) : (lift fo fc).obj (of a) = fo a := rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_tensor (X Y : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).obj (X ⊗ Y) = (lift fo fc).obj X ⊗ (lift fo fc).obj Y := rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_tensorUnit : (lift fo fc).obj (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid) = 𝟙_ D := rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_rightDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).obj (Xᘁ) = ((lift fo fc).obj X)ᘁ := rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_obj_leftDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).obj (ᘁX) = ᘁ((lift fo fc).obj X) := rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_coupon (g : S.Coupon) : (lift fo fc).map (coupon g) = fc g := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_whiskerLeft (X : S.FreeRigid) {Y₁ Y₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : Y₁ ⟶ Y₂) :
    (lift fo fc).map (X ◁ f) = (lift fo fc).obj X ◁ (lift fo fc).map f := by
  induction f using Quotient.inductionOn
  rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_whiskerRight {X₁ X₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : X₁ ⟶ X₂) (Y : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (f ▷ Y) = (lift fo fc).map f ▷ (lift fo fc).obj Y := by
  induction f using Quotient.inductionOn
  rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_tensorHom {X₁ Y₁ X₂ Y₂ : S.FreeRigid} (f : X₁ ⟶ Y₁) (g : X₂ ⟶ Y₂) :
    (lift fo fc).map (f ⊗ₘ g) = (lift fo fc).map f ⊗ₘ (lift fo fc).map g := by
  induction f using Quotient.inductionOn
  induction g using Quotient.inductionOn
  rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_associator_hom (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (α_ X Y Z).hom =
      (α_ ((lift fo fc).obj X) ((lift fo fc).obj Y) ((lift fo fc).obj Z)).hom := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_associator_inv (X Y Z : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (α_ X Y Z).inv =
      (α_ ((lift fo fc).obj X) ((lift fo fc).obj Y) ((lift fo fc).obj Z)).inv := by rfl

/- The unitor lemmas are not `@[simp]`: Mathlib's `Functor.LaxMonoidal.left_unitality` and
`right_unitality` rewrite their right-hand sides back into `(lift fo fc).map` of a unitor. -/
theorem lift_map_leftUnitor_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (λ_ X).hom = (λ_ ((lift fo fc).obj X)).hom := by rfl

theorem lift_map_leftUnitor_inv (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (λ_ X).inv = (λ_ ((lift fo fc).obj X)).inv := by rfl

theorem lift_map_rightUnitor_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (ρ_ X).hom = (ρ_ ((lift fo fc).obj X)).hom := by rfl

theorem lift_map_rightUnitor_inv (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (ρ_ X).inv = (ρ_ ((lift fo fc).obj X)).inv := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_rightCoevaluation (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (η_ X (Xᘁ)) = η_ ((lift fo fc).obj X) (((lift fo fc).obj X)ᘁ) := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_rightEvaluation (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (ε_ X (Xᘁ)) = ε_ ((lift fo fc).obj X) (((lift fo fc).obj X)ᘁ) := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_leftCoevaluation (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (η_ (ᘁX) X) = η_ (ᘁ((lift fo fc).obj X)) ((lift fo fc).obj X) := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_map_leftEvaluation (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).map (ε_ (ᘁX) X) = ε_ (ᘁ((lift fo fc).obj X)) ((lift fo fc).obj X) := by rfl

noncomputable instance : (lift fo fc).Monoidal :=
  Functor.CoreMonoidal.toMonoidal
    { εIso := Iso.refl _
      μIso := fun _ _ ↦ Iso.refl _
      μIso_hom_natural_left := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor]
        simp
      μIso_hom_natural_right := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor]
        simp
      associativity := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor]
        simp
      left_unitality := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor, lift_obj_tensorUnit]
        simp [lift_map_leftUnitor_hom]
      right_unitality := by
        intros
        dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_tensor, lift_obj_tensorUnit]
        simp [lift_map_rightUnitor_hom] }

@[simp]
theorem lift_ε : Functor.LaxMonoidal.ε (lift fo fc) = 𝟙 _ := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_η : Functor.OplaxMonoidal.η (lift fo fc) = 𝟙 _ := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_μ (X Y : S.FreeRigid) : Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ (lift fo fc) X Y = 𝟙 _ := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem lift_δ (X Y : S.FreeRigid) : Functor.OplaxMonoidal.δ (lift fo fc) X Y = 𝟙 _ := by rfl

/-- Because `lift fo fc` strictly preserves chosen right duals and their evaluations, its right-dual
comparison isomorphism is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_mapRightDualIso (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).mapRightDualIso X (_hFX := RightRigidCategory.rightDual ((lift fo fc).obj X)) =
      Iso.refl _ := by
  ext
  refine ExactPairing.rightHom_ext
    (X := (lift fo fc).obj X)
    (Y := @HasRightDual.rightDual _ _ _ ((lift fo fc).obj X) (RightRigidCategory.rightDual _)) ?_
  refine ((lift fo fc).mapRightDualIso_hom_whiskerRight_evaluation X
    (_hFX := RightRigidCategory.rightDual _)).trans ?_
  dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_rightDual]
  simp

/-- Because `lift fo fc` strictly preserves chosen left duals and their evaluations, its left-dual
comparison isomorphism is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_mapLeftDualIso (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (lift fo fc).mapLeftDualIso X (_hFY := LeftRigidCategory.leftDual ((lift fo fc).obj X)) =
      Iso.refl _ := by
  ext
  refine ExactPairing.leftDualHom_ext
    (X := @HasLeftDual.leftDual _ _ _ ((lift fo fc).obj X) (LeftRigidCategory.leftDual _))
    (Y := (lift fo fc).obj X) ?_
  refine ((lift fo fc).whiskerLeft_mapLeftDualIso_hom_evaluation X
    (_hFY := LeftRigidCategory.leftDual _)).trans ?_
  dsimp only [Iso.refl_hom, lift_obj_leftDual]
  simp

end Lift

section Uniqueness

open Functor.LaxMonoidal Functor.OplaxMonoidal

/-- A monoidal natural transformation from a strong monoidal functor out of `S.FreeRigid` to a lax
monoidal functor into an arbitrary monoidal category is determined by its components at the
generating objects. No rigidity assumption on the target category `D` is required. -/
theorem natTrans_ext {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [MonoidalCategory D]
    {F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D} [F.Monoidal] [G.LaxMonoidal] {α β : F ⟶ G}
    [NatTrans.IsMonoidal α] [NatTrans.IsMonoidal β] (h : ∀ a, α.app (of a) = β.app (of a)) :
    α = β := by
  ext ⟨X⟩
  induction X with
  | of a => exact h a
  | unit =>
    rw [← cancel_epi (ε F)]
    exact (NatTrans.IsMonoidal.unit (τ := α)).trans (NatTrans.IsMonoidal.unit (τ := β)).symm
  | tensor X Y hX hY =>
    rw [← cancel_epi (μ F ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩)]
    refine (NatTrans.IsMonoidal.tensor (τ := α) ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩).trans ?_
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (NatTrans.IsMonoidal.tensor (τ := β) ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩).symm
    rw [hX, hY]
  | rightDual X hX =>
    exact NatTrans.app_right_eq_of_exactPairing (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ((⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)ᘁ) hX
  | leftDual X hX =>
    exact NatTrans.app_left_eq_of_exactPairing (ᘁ(⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)) (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) hX

variable {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [MonoidalCategory D] [RigidCategory D]
variable (F G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D) [F.Monoidal] [G.Monoidal] (e : ∀ a, F.obj (of a) ≅ G.obj (of a))

/-- The canonical isomorphism between the images of a formal rigid object expression under two
strong monoidal functors `F, G : S.FreeRigid ⥤ D`, built from isomorphisms `e` at the generating
objects together with the unit, tensor, right-dual and left-dual comparisons of `F` and `G`. -/
noncomputable def objIso : ∀ X : RigidObject S.Obj, F.obj ⟨X⟩ ≅ G.obj ⟨X⟩
  | .of a => e a
  | .unit => (Functor.Monoidal.εIso F).symm ≪≫ Functor.Monoidal.εIso G
  | .tensor X Y =>
    (Functor.Monoidal.μIso F ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩).symm ≪≫ (objIso X ⊗ᵢ objIso Y) ≪≫
      Functor.Monoidal.μIso G ⟨X⟩ ⟨Y⟩
  | .rightDual X =>
    F.mapRightDualIso (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ≪≫ (objIso X).symm.rightAdjointMate ≪≫
      (G.mapRightDualIso (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)).symm
  | .leftDual X =>
    F.mapLeftDualIso (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid) ≪≫ (objIso X).symm.leftAdjointMate ≪≫
      (G.mapLeftDualIso (⟨X⟩ : S.FreeRigid)).symm

@[simp]
theorem objIso_of (a : S.Obj) : objIso F G e (of a).as = e a := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem objIso_tensorUnit_hom : (objIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom = η F ≫ ε G := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem objIso_tensorUnit_inv : (objIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).inv = η G ≫ ε F := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem objIso_tensor_hom (X Y : S.FreeRigid) :
    (objIso F G e (X ⊗ Y).as).hom =
      δ F X Y ≫ ((objIso F G e X.as).hom ⊗ₘ (objIso F G e Y.as).hom) ≫ μ G X Y := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem objIso_tensor_inv (X Y : S.FreeRigid) :
    (objIso F G e (X ⊗ Y).as).inv =
      δ G X Y ≫ ((objIso F G e X.as).inv ⊗ₘ (objIso F G e Y.as).inv) ≫ μ F X Y :=
  Category.assoc _ _ _

theorem objIso_rightDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    objIso F G e (Xᘁ).as =
      F.mapRightDualIso X ≪≫ (objIso F G e X.as).symm.rightAdjointMate ≪≫
        (G.mapRightDualIso X).symm := by
  rfl

theorem objIso_leftDual (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    objIso F G e (ᘁX).as =
      F.mapLeftDualIso X ≪≫ (objIso F G e X.as).symm.leftAdjointMate ≪≫
        (G.mapLeftDualIso X).symm := by
  rfl

@[simp]
theorem objIso_rightDual_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (objIso F G e (Xᘁ).as).hom =
      (F.mapRightDualIso X).hom ≫ ((objIso F G e X.as).inv)ᘁ ≫ (G.mapRightDualIso X).inv := by
  rw [objIso_rightDual]
  simp

@[simp]
theorem objIso_leftDual_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (objIso F G e (ᘁX).as).hom =
      (F.mapLeftDualIso X).hom ≫ (ᘁ(objIso F G e X.as).inv) ≫ (G.mapLeftDualIso X).inv := by
  rw [objIso_leftDual]
  simp

variable {F G e}

attribute [local simp] whiskerLeft_comp_tensorHom whiskerLeft_comp_tensorHom_assoc
  whiskerRight_comp_tensorHom whiskerRight_comp_tensorHom_assoc tensorHom_comp_whiskerLeft
  tensorHom_comp_whiskerLeft_assoc tensorHom_comp_whiskerRight tensorHom_comp_whiskerRight_assoc

private theorem map_rightCoevaluation_comp_objIso_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    F.map (η_ X (Xᘁ)) ≫ (objIso F G e (X ⊗ Xᘁ).as).hom =
      (objIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom ≫ G.map (η_ X (Xᘁ)) := by
  rw [← cancel_epi (ε F), ← cancel_mono (δ G X (Xᘁ))]
  simp only [objIso_tensor_hom, objIso_rightDual_hom, objIso_tensorUnit_hom, Category.assoc,
    Functor.Monoidal.μ_δ, Category.comp_id, Functor.Monoidal.ε_η_assoc]
  rw [← F.coevaluation_whiskerLeft_mapRightDualIso_inv_assoc X,
    ← G.coevaluation_whiskerLeft_mapRightDualIso_inv X,
    whiskerLeft_comp_tensorHom, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc,
    tensorHom_def' (objIso F G e X.as).hom, MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_comp_assoc,
    coevaluation_comp_rightAdjointMate_assoc, whisker_exchange,
    ← comp_whiskerRight_assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, MonoidalCategory.id_whiskerRight, Category.id_comp]

private theorem map_rightEvaluation_comp_objIso_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    F.map (ε_ X (Xᘁ)) ≫ (objIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom =
      (objIso F G e (Xᘁ ⊗ X).as).hom ≫ G.map (ε_ X (Xᘁ)) := by
  rw [← cancel_epi (μ F (Xᘁ) X), ← cancel_mono (η G)]
  simp only [objIso_tensor_hom, objIso_rightDual_hom, objIso_tensorUnit_hom, Category.assoc,
    Functor.Monoidal.μ_δ_assoc, Functor.Monoidal.ε_η, Category.comp_id]
  rw [← F.mapRightDualIso_hom_whiskerRight_evaluation X,
    ← G.mapRightDualIso_hom_whiskerRight_evaluation X,
    tensorHom_comp_whiskerRight_assoc]
  simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.comp_id]
  rw [tensorHom_def' ((F.mapRightDualIso X).hom ≫ ((objIso F G e X.as).inv)ᘁ),
    comp_whiskerRight, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, rightAdjointMate_comp_evaluation,
    ← whisker_exchange_assoc, ← MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_comp_assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id,
    MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_id, Category.id_comp]

private theorem map_leftCoevaluation_comp_objIso_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    F.map (η_ (ᘁX) X) ≫ (objIso F G e ((ᘁX) ⊗ X).as).hom =
      (objIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom ≫ G.map (η_ (ᘁX) X) := by
  rw [← cancel_epi (ε F), ← cancel_mono (δ G (ᘁX) X)]
  simp only [objIso_tensor_hom, objIso_leftDual_hom, objIso_tensorUnit_hom, Category.assoc,
    Functor.Monoidal.μ_δ, Category.comp_id, Functor.Monoidal.ε_η_assoc]
  rw [← F.coevaluation_mapLeftDualIso_inv_whiskerRight_assoc X,
    ← G.coevaluation_mapLeftDualIso_inv_whiskerRight X,
    whiskerRight_comp_tensorHom, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc,
    MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def, comp_whiskerRight_assoc,
    coevaluation_comp_leftAdjointMate_assoc, ← whisker_exchange,
    ← MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_comp_assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_id,
    Category.id_comp]

private theorem map_leftEvaluation_comp_objIso_hom (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    F.map (ε_ (ᘁX) X) ≫ (objIso F G e (𝟙_ S.FreeRigid).as).hom =
      (objIso F G e (X ⊗ ᘁX).as).hom ≫ G.map (ε_ (ᘁX) X) := by
  rw [← cancel_epi (μ F X (ᘁX)), ← cancel_mono (η G)]
  simp only [objIso_tensor_hom, objIso_leftDual_hom, objIso_tensorUnit_hom, Category.assoc,
    Functor.Monoidal.μ_δ_assoc, Functor.Monoidal.ε_η, Category.comp_id]
  rw [← F.whiskerLeft_mapLeftDualIso_hom_evaluation X,
    ← G.whiskerLeft_mapLeftDualIso_hom_evaluation X,
    tensorHom_comp_whiskerLeft_assoc]
  simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.comp_id]
  rw [MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def (objIso F G e X.as).hom,
    MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_comp, Category.assoc, Category.assoc,
    leftAdjointMate_comp_evaluation, whisker_exchange_assoc, ← comp_whiskerRight_assoc,
    Iso.hom_inv_id, MonoidalCategory.id_whiskerRight, Category.id_comp]

/-- The family `objIso F G e` is natural with respect to all morphisms of `S.FreeRigid` as soon as
it is natural with respect to every coupon. -/
theorem map_comp_objIso_hom
    (he : ∀ g, F.map (coupon g) ≫ (objIso F G e (S.tgt g)).hom =
      (objIso F G e (S.src g)).hom ≫ G.map (coupon g))
    {X Y : S.FreeRigid} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    F.map f ≫ (objIso F G e Y.as).hom = (objIso F G e X.as).hom ≫ G.map f := by
  induction f using Hom.inductionOn with
  | id X => simp
  | α_hom X Y Z =>
    rw [← cancel_epi (μ F X Y ▷ F.obj Z ≫ μ F (X ⊗ Y) Z),
      ← cancel_mono (δ G X (Y ⊗ Z) ≫ G.obj X ◁ δ G Y Z)]
    simp [← Functor.OplaxMonoidal.associativity]
  | α_inv X Y Z =>
    rw [← cancel_epi (F.obj X ◁ μ F Y Z ≫ μ F X (Y ⊗ Z)),
      ← cancel_mono (δ G (X ⊗ Y) Z ≫ δ G X Y ▷ G.obj Z)]
    simp [← Functor.OplaxMonoidal.associativity_inv]
  | l_hom X =>
    rw [← cancel_epi (ε F ▷ F.obj X ≫ μ F (𝟙_ _) X)]
    simp
    simp [tensorHom_def']
  | l_inv X =>
    rw [← cancel_mono (δ G (𝟙_ _) X ≫ η G ▷ G.obj X)]
    simp
    simp [MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def, ← Functor.OplaxMonoidal.left_unitality]
  | ρ_hom X =>
    rw [← cancel_epi (F.obj X ◁ ε F ≫ μ F X (𝟙_ _))]
    simp
    simp [MonoidalCategory.tensorHom_def]
  | ρ_inv X =>
    rw [← cancel_mono (δ G X (𝟙_ _) ≫ G.obj X ◁ η G)]
    simp
    simp [tensorHom_def', ← Functor.OplaxMonoidal.right_unitality]
  | rightCoevaluation X => exact map_rightCoevaluation_comp_objIso_hom X
  | rightEvaluation X => exact map_rightEvaluation_comp_objIso_hom X
  | leftCoevaluation X => exact map_leftCoevaluation_comp_objIso_hom X
  | leftEvaluation X => exact map_leftEvaluation_comp_objIso_hom X
  | coupon g => exact he g
  | comp f g hf hg =>
    rw [Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc, hg, reassoc_of% hf]
  | whiskerLeft X f hf =>
    simp only [objIso_tensor_hom, Functor.Monoidal.map_whiskerLeft, Category.assoc,
      Functor.Monoidal.μ_δ_assoc, whiskerLeft_comp_tensorHom_assoc,
      tensorHom_comp_whiskerLeft_assoc, hf]
  | whiskerRight f X hf =>
    simp only [objIso_tensor_hom, Functor.Monoidal.map_whiskerRight, Category.assoc,
      Functor.Monoidal.μ_δ_assoc, whiskerRight_comp_tensorHom_assoc,
      tensorHom_comp_whiskerRight_assoc, hf]

/-- Two strong monoidal functors out of `S.FreeRigid` into a rigid monoidal category `D` that agree
up to isomorphisms `e` on the generating objects, compatibly with every coupon, are isomorphic by a
monoidal natural isomorphism extending `e`. -/
noncomputable def monoidalNatIso
    (he : ∀ g, F.map (coupon g) ≫ (objIso F G e (S.tgt g)).hom =
      (objIso F G e (S.src g)).hom ≫ G.map (coupon g)) :
    F ≅ G :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun X ↦ objIso F G e X.as) fun f ↦ map_comp_objIso_hom he f

variable (he : ∀ g, F.map (coupon g) ≫ (objIso F G e (S.tgt g)).hom =
  (objIso F G e (S.src g)).hom ≫ G.map (coupon g))

@[simp]
theorem monoidalNatIso_hom_app (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (monoidalNatIso he).hom.app X = (objIso F G e X.as).hom := by rfl

@[simp]
theorem monoidalNatIso_inv_app (X : S.FreeRigid) :
    (monoidalNatIso he).inv.app X = (objIso F G e X.as).inv := by rfl

theorem monoidalNatIso_hom_app_of (a : S.Obj) :
    (monoidalNatIso he).hom.app (of a) = (e a).hom := by rfl

theorem monoidalNatIso_inv_app_of (a : S.Obj) :
    (monoidalNatIso he).inv.app (of a) = (e a).inv := by rfl

instance : NatTrans.IsMonoidal (monoidalNatIso he).hom where
  unit := by
    rw [monoidalNatIso_hom_app, objIso_tensorUnit_hom, Functor.Monoidal.ε_η_assoc]
  tensor X Y := by
    rw [monoidalNatIso_hom_app, objIso_tensor_hom, Functor.Monoidal.μ_δ_assoc,
      monoidalNatIso_hom_app, monoidalNatIso_hom_app]

/-- Uniqueness of the monoidal natural isomorphism extending `e` on the generating objects. -/
theorem eq_monoidalNatIso {α : F ≅ G} [NatTrans.IsMonoidal α.hom]
    (hα : ∀ a, α.hom.app (of a) = (e a).hom) :
    α = monoidalNatIso he := by
  ext1
  exact natTrans_ext fun a ↦ (hα a).trans (monoidalNatIso_hom_app_of he a).symm

end Uniqueness

section NonPivotal

/-!
### Non-pivotality of the free rigid category on a coupon-free signature

To show that `S.FreeRigid` does not identify a generating object `of a` with its double right dual
`((of a)ᘁ)ᘁ` or double left dual `ᘁ(ᘁ(of a))` when `S.Coupon` is empty, we interpret `S.FreeRigid`
into a small thin rigid category `LambekObj` of 2-periodic monotone integer maps `ℤ → ℤ` (a concrete
Lambek pregroup). Sending `a` to `n ↦ 2 * (n / 2)` maps `of a` to `(0, 0)` and `((of a)ᘁ)ᘁ` to
`(-1, 1)`, which are incomparable in the pointwise order.
-/

/-- A 2-periodic monotone map `ℤ → ℤ`, represented by its values `(ev, od)` at `0` and `1` with
`ev ≤ od ≤ ev + 2`. -/
@[ext]
private structure LambekObj where
  ev : ℤ
  od : ℤ
  ev_le_od : ev ≤ od
  od_le_ev_add_two : od ≤ ev + 2

namespace LambekObj

private def eval (x : LambekObj) (n : ℤ) : ℤ :=
  2 * (n / 2) + if n % 2 = 0 then x.ev else x.od

private theorem eval_mono (x : LambekObj) {m n : ℤ} (h : m ≤ n) : x.eval m ≤ x.eval n := by
  have := x.ev_le_od
  have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
  dsimp only [eval]
  omega

private instance : PartialOrder LambekObj where
  le x y := x.ev ≤ y.ev ∧ x.od ≤ y.od
  le_refl x := ⟨le_rfl, le_rfl⟩
  le_trans _ _ _ h₁ h₂ := ⟨h₁.1.trans h₂.1, h₁.2.trans h₂.2⟩
  le_antisymm _ _ h₁ h₂ := LambekObj.ext (le_antisymm h₁.1 h₂.1) (le_antisymm h₁.2 h₂.2)

private theorem le_iff_eval_le {x y : LambekObj} : x ≤ y ↔ ∀ n, x.eval n ≤ y.eval n := by
  refine ⟨fun ⟨hev, hod⟩ n ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  · dsimp only [eval]
    omega
  · have h0 := h 0
    have h1 := h 1
    dsimp only [eval] at h0 h1
    exact ⟨by omega, by omega⟩

private def one : LambekObj where
  ev := 0
  od := 1
  ev_le_od := by omega
  od_le_ev_add_two := by omega

private theorem one_eval (n : ℤ) : one.eval n = n := by
  dsimp only [one, eval]
  omega

private def mul (x y : LambekObj) : LambekObj where
  ev := x.eval y.ev
  od := x.eval y.od
  ev_le_od := x.eval_mono y.ev_le_od
  od_le_ev_add_two := by
    have := x.ev_le_od
    have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
    have := y.ev_le_od
    have := y.od_le_ev_add_two
    dsimp only [eval]
    omega

private theorem mul_eval (x y : LambekObj) (n : ℤ) : (mul x y).eval n = x.eval (y.eval n) := by
  have := x.ev_le_od
  have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
  dsimp only [mul, eval]
  omega

private def rdual (x : LambekObj) : LambekObj where
  ev := min (2 * ((-x.ev + 1) / 2)) (2 * ((-x.od + 1) / 2) + 1)
  od := min (2 * ((2 - x.ev) / 2)) (2 * ((2 - x.od) / 2) + 1)
  ev_le_od := by
    have := x.ev_le_od
    have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
    omega
  od_le_ev_add_two := by
    have := x.ev_le_od
    have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
    omega

private theorem rdual_coev (x : LambekObj) : one ≤ mul x (rdual x) := by
  rw [le_iff_eval_le]
  intro n
  rw [one_eval, mul_eval]
  have := x.ev_le_od
  have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
  dsimp only [rdual, eval]
  omega

private theorem rdual_ev (x : LambekObj) : mul (rdual x) x ≤ one := by
  rw [le_iff_eval_le]
  intro n
  rw [one_eval, mul_eval]
  have := x.ev_le_od
  have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
  dsimp only [rdual, eval]
  omega

private def ldual (x : LambekObj) : LambekObj where
  ev := max (2 * ((-x.ev) / 2)) (2 * ((-x.od) / 2) + 1)
  od := max (2 * ((1 - x.ev) / 2)) (2 * ((1 - x.od) / 2) + 1)
  ev_le_od := by
    have := x.ev_le_od
    have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
    omega
  od_le_ev_add_two := by
    have := x.ev_le_od
    have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
    omega

private theorem ldual_coev (x : LambekObj) : one ≤ mul (ldual x) x := by
  rw [le_iff_eval_le]
  intro n
  rw [one_eval, mul_eval]
  have := x.ev_le_od
  have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
  dsimp only [ldual, eval]
  omega

private theorem ldual_ev (x : LambekObj) : mul x (ldual x) ≤ one := by
  rw [le_iff_eval_le]
  intro n
  rw [one_eval, mul_eval]
  have := x.ev_le_od
  have := x.od_le_ev_add_two
  dsimp only [ldual, eval]
  omega

private instance : MonoidalCategory LambekObj where
  tensorObj := mul
  whiskerLeft X _ _ f := homOfLE <| le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by
    rw [mul_eval, mul_eval]
    exact X.eval_mono (le_iff_eval_le.1 (leOfHom f) n)
  whiskerRight f Y := homOfLE <| le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by
    rw [mul_eval, mul_eval]
    exact le_iff_eval_le.1 (leOfHom f) (Y.eval n)
  tensorHom {X₁ Y₁ X₂ Y₂} f g := homOfLE <| le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by
    rw [mul_eval, mul_eval]
    exact (le_iff_eval_le.1 (leOfHom f) (X₂.eval n)).trans
      (Y₁.eval_mono (le_iff_eval_le.1 (leOfHom g) n))
  tensorUnit := one
  associator X Y Z := eqToIso <| le_antisymm
    (le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by simp only [mul_eval]; exact le_rfl)
    (le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by simp only [mul_eval]; exact le_rfl)
  leftUnitor X := eqToIso <| le_antisymm
    (le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by simp only [mul_eval, one_eval]; exact le_rfl)
    (le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by simp only [mul_eval, one_eval]; exact le_rfl)
  rightUnitor X := eqToIso <| le_antisymm
    (le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by simp only [mul_eval, one_eval]; exact le_rfl)
    (le_iff_eval_le.2 fun n ↦ by simp only [mul_eval, one_eval]; exact le_rfl)

private instance instRightRigidLambekObj : RightRigidCategory LambekObj where
  rightDual X :=
    { rightDual := rdual X
      exact :=
        { coevaluation' := homOfLE (rdual_coev X)
          evaluation' := homOfLE (rdual_ev X) } }

private instance instLeftRigidLambekObj : LeftRigidCategory LambekObj where
  leftDual X :=
    { leftDual := ldual X
      exact :=
        { coevaluation' := homOfLE (ldual_coev X)
          evaluation' := homOfLE (ldual_ev X) } }

private instance : RigidCategory LambekObj where

private def base : LambekObj where
  ev := 0
  od := 0
  ev_le_od := by omega
  od_le_ev_add_two := by omega

end LambekObj

/-- In the free rigid category on a coupon-free duality signature, there is no morphism from a
generating object `of a` to its double right dual `((of a)ᘁ)ᘁ`. -/
theorem isEmpty_hom_of_doubleRightDual [IsEmpty S.Coupon] (a : S.Obj) :
    IsEmpty (of a ⟶ ((of a)ᘁ)ᘁ) := by
  refine ⟨fun f ↦ ?_⟩
  let F : S.FreeRigid ⥤ LambekObj := lift (fun _ ↦ LambekObj.base) isEmptyElim
  have hle : LambekObj.base ≤ LambekObj.rdual (LambekObj.rdual LambekObj.base) := leOfHom (F.map f)
  have hev := hle.1
  dsimp only [LambekObj.rdual, LambekObj.base] at hev
  omega

/-- In the free rigid category on a coupon-free duality signature, there is no morphism from the
double right dual `((of a)ᘁ)ᘁ` of a generating object back to `of a`. -/
theorem isEmpty_hom_doubleRightDual_of [IsEmpty S.Coupon] (a : S.Obj) :
    IsEmpty (((of a)ᘁ)ᘁ ⟶ of a) := by
  refine ⟨fun f ↦ ?_⟩
  let F : S.FreeRigid ⥤ LambekObj := lift (fun _ ↦ LambekObj.base) isEmptyElim
  have hle : LambekObj.rdual (LambekObj.rdual LambekObj.base) ≤ LambekObj.base := leOfHom (F.map f)
  have hod := hle.2
  dsimp only [LambekObj.rdual, LambekObj.base] at hod
  omega

/-- In the free rigid category on a coupon-free duality signature, no generating object is
isomorphic to its double right dual. -/
theorem isEmpty_iso_of_doubleRightDual [IsEmpty S.Coupon] (a : S.Obj) :
    IsEmpty (of a ≅ ((of a)ᘁ)ᘁ) :=
  ⟨fun e ↦ (isEmpty_hom_of_doubleRightDual a).false e.hom⟩

/-- In the free rigid category on a coupon-free duality signature, there is no morphism from a
generating object `of a` to its double left dual `ᘁ(ᘁ(of a))`. -/
theorem isEmpty_hom_of_doubleLeftDual [IsEmpty S.Coupon] (a : S.Obj) :
    IsEmpty (of a ⟶ ᘁ(ᘁ(of a))) := by
  refine ⟨fun f ↦ ?_⟩
  let F : S.FreeRigid ⥤ LambekObj := lift (fun _ ↦ LambekObj.base) isEmptyElim
  have hle : LambekObj.base ≤ LambekObj.ldual (LambekObj.ldual LambekObj.base) := leOfHom (F.map f)
  have hev := hle.1
  dsimp only [LambekObj.ldual, LambekObj.base] at hev
  omega

/-- In the free rigid category on a coupon-free duality signature, there is no morphism from the
double left dual `ᘁ(ᘁ(of a))` of a generating object back to `of a`. -/
theorem isEmpty_hom_doubleLeftDual_of [IsEmpty S.Coupon] (a : S.Obj) :
    IsEmpty ((ᘁ(ᘁ(of a))) ⟶ of a) := by
  refine ⟨fun f ↦ ?_⟩
  let F : S.FreeRigid ⥤ LambekObj := lift (fun _ ↦ LambekObj.base) isEmptyElim
  have hle : LambekObj.ldual (LambekObj.ldual LambekObj.base) ≤ LambekObj.base := leOfHom (F.map f)
  have hod := hle.2
  dsimp only [LambekObj.ldual, LambekObj.base] at hod
  omega

/-- In the free rigid category on a coupon-free duality signature, no generating object is
isomorphic to its double left dual. -/
theorem isEmpty_iso_of_doubleLeftDual [IsEmpty S.Coupon] (a : S.Obj) :
    IsEmpty (of a ≅ ᘁ(ᘁ(of a))) :=
  ⟨fun e ↦ (isEmpty_hom_of_doubleLeftDual a).false e.hom⟩

end NonPivotal

end FreeRigid

end DualitySignature

namespace TensorSignature.FreeMonoidal

variable (S : TensorSignature.{u, v})

/-- Interpreting a dual-free monoidal word via the generating objects of
`S.toDualitySignature.FreeRigid` produces the object whose underlying `RigidObject` is
`W.toRigidObject`. -/
@[simp]
theorem projectObj_of_eq (W : FreeMonoidalCategory S.Obj) :
    FreeMonoidalCategory.projectObj
        (fun a : S.Obj ↦ DualitySignature.FreeRigid.of (S := S.toDualitySignature) a) W =
      ⟨W.toRigidObject⟩ :=
  (RigidObject.projectObj_toRigidObject _ W).symm.trans
    (DualitySignature.FreeRigid.projectObj_of_eq (S := S.toDualitySignature) W.toRigidObject)

/-- The canonical strong monoidal functor embedding the free monoidal category on a tensor signature
`S` into the free rigid category on `S.toDualitySignature`, obtained by the universal lift of
`FreeMonoidal`. -/
@[expose] def toFreeRigid : S.FreeMonoidal ⥤ S.toDualitySignature.FreeRigid :=
  FreeMonoidal.lift
    (fun a : S.Obj ↦ DualitySignature.FreeRigid.of (S := S.toDualitySignature) a) fun g ↦
      eqToHom (projectObj_of_eq S (S.src g)) ≫
        DualitySignature.FreeRigid.coupon (S := S.toDualitySignature) g ≫
        eqToHom (projectObj_of_eq S (S.tgt g)).symm

instance : (toFreeRigid S).Monoidal :=
  inferInstanceAs
    (FreeMonoidal.lift
      (fun a : S.Obj ↦ DualitySignature.FreeRigid.of (S := S.toDualitySignature) a) fun g ↦
        eqToHom (projectObj_of_eq S (S.src g)) ≫
          DualitySignature.FreeRigid.coupon (S := S.toDualitySignature) g ≫
          eqToHom (projectObj_of_eq S (S.tgt g)).symm).Monoidal

@[simp]
theorem toFreeRigid_obj (X : S.FreeMonoidal) :
    (toFreeRigid S).obj X = ⟨X.as.toRigidObject⟩ :=
  projectObj_of_eq S X.as

@[simp]
theorem toFreeRigid_obj_of (a : S.Obj) :
    (toFreeRigid S).obj (of a) = DualitySignature.FreeRigid.of a := rfl

theorem toFreeRigid_map_coupon (g : S.Coupon) :
    (toFreeRigid S).map (coupon g) =
      eqToHom (toFreeRigid_obj S ⟨S.src g⟩) ≫
        DualitySignature.FreeRigid.coupon (S := S.toDualitySignature) g ≫
        eqToHom (toFreeRigid_obj S ⟨S.tgt g⟩).symm :=
  FreeMonoidal.lift_map_coupon _ _ g

@[simp]
theorem toFreeRigid_ε : Functor.LaxMonoidal.ε (toFreeRigid S) = 𝟙 _ :=
  FreeMonoidal.lift_ε _ _

@[simp]
theorem toFreeRigid_η : Functor.OplaxMonoidal.η (toFreeRigid S) = 𝟙 _ :=
  FreeMonoidal.lift_η _ _

@[simp]
theorem toFreeRigid_μ (X Y : S.FreeMonoidal) :
    Functor.LaxMonoidal.μ (toFreeRigid S) X Y = 𝟙 _ :=
  FreeMonoidal.lift_μ _ _ X Y

@[simp]
theorem toFreeRigid_δ (X Y : S.FreeMonoidal) :
    Functor.OplaxMonoidal.δ (toFreeRigid S) X Y = 𝟙 _ :=
  FreeMonoidal.lift_δ _ _ X Y

end TensorSignature.FreeMonoidal

end TauCeti
